==Trivia==
*Originally, Baozi Cat was a Taiwanese exclusive unit unlocked through clearing [[Secret Delicacy]]. However, in [[Version 11.2 Update|Version 11.2]] it was introduced in the [[Lunar New Year (Event Gacha)|Lunar New Year]] Event Gacha for the Japanese version, and in [[Version 15.1 Update|Version 15.1]] it was added to that same Event Gacha globally.
*Despite not being obtainable in the English or Korean versions up until Version 15.1, it had fully translated descriptions, suggesting that there may have been plans to add it globally before 15.1.
*When Baozi Cat released globally in Version 15.1, the French, Italian, German, Spanish and Thai languages of the English Version had no descriptions. This was fixed in Version 15.1.1.
*It, [[Nekondo (Special Cat)|Nekondo]], [[Crazed Baozi Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Baozi Cat]], [[Li'l Valkyrie (Uber Rare Cat)|Li'l Valkyrie]], and [[Li'l Valkyrie Dark (Uber Rare Cat)|Li'l Valkyrie Dark]] are part of a version exclusive in The Battle Cats Unite, only being available for those who own the Southeast Asia version.
**It is present in the Japanese version, however, it requires save file modification in order to be playable.
*Baozi Cat in The Battle Cats Unite! has a maximum level up 30+20, however the +20 level cap is impossible to view naturally and is obtainable via save file editing.
*Much like [[Coastal Explorer Kanna (Uber Rare Cat)|Coastal Explorer Kanna]], Baozi Cat has an unused description and name for its True Form present in the Japanese Mobile Version. However, this is likely a mistake, because the name and description are both identical to the Evolved Form's in the Japanese Switch Version.
